  "final_text": "**No. Drop it from the shelf card as it stands.** It fails on two separate grounds, and fixing one wouldn't fix the other.\n\n| No | Claim | Answer | File and line | Status | Reason | Missing document | Action |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | \"Certified organic vineyards\" next to all wines | No | organic_certificate_vineyard.txt:6, :8, :9, :10, :11; company_profile.md:7 | GAP | **Scope:** only 12.0 of 40 ha are certified (:6), \"the other 28 ha are not certified\" (:10), and \"Cellar and winemaking: not certified\" (:11). Placed next to every wine, the claim covers all 40 ha and all wines, so it hits ban item **4b** (a claim about the whole when only part qualifies). **Period:** the certificate was valid until 31.08.2026 (:8). On your reference date of 16.10.2026, even the 12 ha are uncertified. The renewal inspection is only booked for 22.10.2026 (:9). | (1) A renewed organic certificate from Biosertifika Kontrola (XX-BIO-000) valid on the shelf-card date. (2) Grape-sourcing records showing which wines come only from the 12 certified ha. | Drop. Don't reprint until the renewal certificate is in the files. |\n\n**Count:** 0 COVERED, 0 WEAK, 1 GAP.\n\n**Documents to request:**\n1. Renewed organic certificate from Biosertifika Kontrola, valid from after 31.08.2026 (row 1)\n2. Grape-sourcing / harvest-to-cuvée records per wine, showing which wines come only from the 12 certified ha (row 1)\n\n**What could go on a card later (only once the renewed certificate is in hand):**\n- Something narrow and dated, such as: *\"12 of our 40 ha of vineyards are certified organic (Biosertifika Kontrola, XX-BIO-000, valid until [date]).\"*\n- It belongs on a general winery card, not next to each wine. Next to a wine it still suggests that the wine itself is organic, and the cellar isn't certified (:11).\n- Calling a specific wine \"organic\" would need the winemaking certified too, not just the vineyard. EU organic labelling rules (Reg. (EU) 2018/848) apply to that separately.\n\nThese are review notes, not legal advice. A person should check and sign off before anything is printed.",
